1. Downward API -> https://kubernetes.io/docs/tasks/inject-data-application/environment-variable-expose-pod-information/

env:
- name: NODE_NAME
  valueFrom:
    fieldRef:
      fieldPath: spec.nodeName
2. Run a command on a container
  - name: mc-pod-2
    image: busybox:1
    command:
    - sh
    - -c
    - |
      while true; do
        date >> /var/log/shared/date.log
        sleep 1
      done
3. shared volume for multicontainer pods

- name: shared-volume 
  emptyDir: {}


4. Get logs from a specific container in multicontainer pod ==> kubectl logs mc-pod -n mc-namespace -c mc-pod-3

5. Install
dpkg -i ./cri-docker_0.3.16.3-0.debian.deb 
systemctl start cri-docker.service 
systemctl enable cri-docker.service (enable to start on boot)

6. expose using nodePort service
kubectl expose deployment hr-web-app --port=8080 --name=hr-web-app-service --type=NodePort service/hr-web-app-service exposed --dry-run=client -o yaml >prasun.yaml 
vi prasun.yaml ==> add nodePort: 30082

7 switch to a namespace
kubectl config set-context --current --namespace=logging-ns

8 For ingress questions , first obtain the name of ingress class => kubectl get ingressclass

